{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make it a legal requirement to display Food Hygiene Ratings in England",
        "additional_details": "Businesses that fail to display their Food Hygiene Rating should face a fine. Mandatory, visible ratings could make the system meaningful, encourage businesses to maintain high hygiene standards, and ensure customers can see a premises\u2019 rating before entering. There should be a clear and consistent penalty for non-compliance.",
        "background": "Displaying a Food Hygiene Rating is a legal requirement in Wales and Northern Ireland, but remains voluntary in England. I believe this should be changed so premises must display their Food Hygiene Rating clearly at site entrances. Customers should clearly know food standards.",
